      "id": "an-invoice-in-a-foreign-currency-and-its-payments-at-other-rates",
      "kind": "foreign_currency_invoice",
      "classification": "differs",
      "reason": "The document currency is built (WP28): the invoice is posted in the base at the rate of its day with the amount in dollars on every line, each payment is taken at the rate of its own day and the difference of a payment is a journal of its own tied to that payment, as the reference system does. It differs on purpose in two things: the gains go to an account of exchange gains and the losses to an account of exchange losses where the reference system keeps one account under current assets (1209), and the amount in dollars of the tax and revenue lines is kept to four decimals, with the cent the conversion rounds put on the revenue, where the reference system shows it to the cent. The payment form has no rate field here either: a payment takes the rate of the table on its day.",
